SparkFS's memory when SparkFS$Memory is not set: SparkFSApp's !Run's, not 64K.

meminit reads SparkFS$Memory as the module starts -- !Run sets it just
before it loads the module, and on RISC OS 5 leaves it -&2000000, a dynamic
area of up to 32 MB.  Unset, meminit takes a fixed 64K of the RMA.  In
the box's ROM the module starts before any !Run has run; !Run's RMEnsure
then finds it there and loads nothing, so !Run's setting would never be
read.  So unset is now what !Run would have set.  A set
SparkFS$Memory is used as before (*RMReInit SparkFS reads it again).

--- a/SparkFS/mem.c
+++ b/SparkFS/mem.c
@@ -538,7 +538,10 @@
 
  err=_kernel_swi(OS_ReadVarVal,&rx,&rx);
 
- if(err || rx.r[4]!=1 || rx.r[2]!=4) size=0x10000;
+ /* ROSGD: in the ROM, SparkFS starts before any !Run can set
+    SparkFS$Memory.  Unset, it is what SparkFSApp's !Run sets on RISC OS 5,
+    -&2000000 -- a dynamic area of up to 32 MB -- not a 64K block of the RMA */
+ if(err || rx.r[4]!=1 || rx.r[2]!=4) size=-0x2000000;
 
  err=NULL;
 
